\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Validation sweeps used to choose the ridge penalty and the KNN neighbour count. Top row: ridge $\alpha $ on a log scale for raw OFF (solid) and raw ON (dashed) input, with validation $R^2$ (left) and RMSE (right); the dotted line marks the selected $\alpha =10^5$. Bottom row: KNN neighbours for the OFF bank, ON bank, and ON calibration. Selection uses mean validation $R^2$; RMSE is shown for comparison. The current code tunes on ON validation sessions, and the OFF curves show the no-stimulation split for reference. PARRM overlaps the raw ridge curves.}}{13}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
